/ Authoring UI for the structured question types. question_builder_controller renders the editor
/ client-side from the hidden config field and re-serialises on every edit, so a normal submit
/ carries question[config] as JSON (parsed onto the jsonb column by QuestionsController#parsed_config).
.tjs-builder data-controller='question-builder' data-question-builder-type-value=@question.question_type
  = f.hidden_field :config, value: @question.config.to_json, data: { 'question-builder-target': 'config' }
  .tjs-builder__editor data-question-builder-target='editor' data-action='input->question-builder#serialize change->question-builder#serialize'
  - if @question.drag_drop?
    .tjs-builder__help
      h3.tjs-builder__help-title How to build a drag-and-drop question
      ol
        li In the Question Text box above, write the sentence and mark each blank with {{1}}, {{2}}, {{3}} and so on — these become the drop zones students fill in.
        li Add one item per draggable tile. The item's text is what the student sees on the tile.
        li
          | For an item that answers a blank, put that blank's number in the
          strong  Blank #(s)
          | field (e.g. 1 for the first blank).
        li
          | An item can answer more than one blank — list the numbers separated by commas (e.g.
          strong  1,3
          | ). Students can reuse the same tile in each of those blanks.
        li
          | Leave the
          strong  Blank #(s)
          | field empty to make an item a distractor — a wrong option that isn't the answer to any blank.
        li Every blank must have an item assigned to it before the question can be saved.
      p.tjs-builder__help-note Example: “The CPU has a {{1}} unit and a {{2}} unit.” with items “control” (Blank 1), “arithmetic logic” (Blank 2) and “storage” (no blank — a distractor).
